          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "f5HO3n",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$fg",
              "content": "The repository header, as the window narrows",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 22,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "I2JwTl",
              "name": "Lede",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "The same rule on a repository, in four steps as room runs out: first the view options move into Display, the List / Board switch with them, while the state filter (Open) stays longest; then Display drops its label to an icon, keeping its name as a tooltip and for screen readers; then the tab group becomes one dropdown showing the current section; last the title is cut, ending in “…”, with the full name in its tooltip. 1–4 switch sections whatever the header shows. A project's header does the same with its saved views (App · Project).",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
