                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Nothing sits at the row's far right edge. Line 1 is the title, then a pull request's number, then the avatars, then the age, each 8 px after the last; a wide window leaves empty space at the end. The number is in the title's size, regular weight and the quieter $fg-2, so a pull request is found by number at a glance; line 2 starts with the repository alone. An issue keeps its full reference on line 2, and a stack, with no single number, shows its count instead. A nested row reads like any other: the same title, only its indent and smaller icon say it belongs to the issue above.",
