                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Expanded from the panel (⇧↵, ↵ on the open row, or the header's button); ⇧↵, the button or Esc goes back to it. When the item view is at least 1000 px wide on a page (1300 px in the panel, F20) it splits in two. Unlike the app's other columns, the two are one $bg-item surface with no line between them. Left, the summary column, 440 px by default: title, state, where the pull request stands, reviews, checks, what it closes, properties, projects. Right, the timeline: description, the whole thread and the composer, the thread filling the column. The two scroll as one, the wheel scrolling them wherever the pointer is; the summary is sticky in that scroll: at the top while it fits the view, and once taller (here Projects runs off the bottom) scrolled until its bottom meets the view's, then kept there. Here the timeline is scrolled past the description, a review cut by the header. On a page the two columns stand in a box of their own, 1424 px by default; this item area is narrower than that, so the box takes the whole width (F19 shows it centred). Its side edges and the edge between the columns are drawn only while hovered, dragged or focused, $accent then, nothing at rest. The summary's edge is dragged from 360 to 560 px, kept on this device. Both columns' content sits 32 px from every edge, so the edge between them lies midway, and their first lines align 32 px under the header. 440 px holds the merge standing's three buttons on one line once they drop their key hints (⇧M, O and D stay in the tooltips and the command menu), and the reviews line drops '1 approval · dkim' (Reviews says it right below). A line that still doesn't fit gives way at its end with an ellipsis: a check's name first.",
