                      "content": "The panel dragged to 1300 px beside My work in a 1920 × 1080 window (sidebar on its rail, so the list keeps 564 px). The item view measures itself, not the window: in the panel it splits from 1300 px of its own width, on a page from 1000 px, so a panel dragged only a little wider stays in one column. Split, it takes the same two columns as the full screen, on one surface with no line between them, but no box: the two take the panel's width. Both columns' content sits 24 px from every edge, 48 px between them: the summary 440 px and the timeline the remaining 860 (812 of thread; the thread at most 920 px, left-aligned). One scroll, the summary sticky in it. The header is the panel's: ⇧↵ or the expand button opens it full screen. Not scrolled: the description opens the timeline. Narrower than 1300 px, the panel goes back to one column (F21).",
