                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Every workflow, one row each: Broken, Pull requests only, No alerts, Passing, Not known yet, Disabled, each while it has rows. Workflows is the fourth section of the repository view, on 4, shown only while the repository is tracked, in the header's tabs (CH72) and, on a phone, under the repository in the places panel (MB270). Its count is the broken workflows, a dash until every workflow is read, none with no workflows or alerts off. The strip of a pull-request-only workflow, or one without alerts, uses quiet red, the same colour as an old break: it failed, and it isn't news. A cancelled run is a short dash with no verdict. The hollow amber tick is a run in progress. Disabled and generated workflows are plain rows. The Alerts bar above the list says which branches and tags raise alerts here, and P opens the repository's settings on Workflow alerts (T16). The toolbar's end holds only the key hints: ↵ Open, → Other runs.",
