                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The same workflow item full screen: ↵ on the row already open in the panel, ⇧↵ or the toolbar's arrangement button from the panel, or ⇧↵ on the Workflows list to skip the panel. The sidebar stays and the list goes. Unlike an issue or a pull request there is no centred box: a workflow is a list of runs and a details column, not text to read, so it fills the page edge to edge. The edge between the runs and the details is a splitter, a 1 px line at rest in the colour of the runs' separators, which end on it (hovered it turns 2 px accent, W30): dragging it, or ←/→ on the focused edge, sets the details from 320 to 640 px, 400 by default, kept on this device, and the runs take the rest; full screen is always two columns, whatever the width. Its content is a list of its own, so the runs have the keyboard: J/K walk them (the cursor is on #4821) and ↵ opens that run (W4a). ⇧J/⇧K step to the next or previous workflow of the list it was opened from, which is why the header's stepper shows ⇧K ⇧J. F opens the latest failed run, whatever its ref. Esc goes back to the panel it was expanded from, its hint reading “Back to the panel”, or to the list when full screen was reached straight from the list (⇧↵), its hint reading “Back to the list”.",
