                  "width": 1440,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 4,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "TDdyQ",
                      "name": "Caption title",
                      "fill": "$fg",
                      "content": "W34 · A passing run, opened at its summary",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "IMeFt",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A successful Deploy run, opened from the workflow's run list. Unlike a failed run (W4a), which opens at the error, a passing run has nothing to point at, so it opens at a summary: every job with its status and how long it took, when each ran, and what the run was. No log is open; the cursor is on the first job and Enter opens its log in the W4a layout. The toolbar reads as a path, fitloop/webapp › Deploy › #4825: Deploy is the way back to the workflow (Esc goes there too). The run is text to read, not a list, so like an item page (D9) it stands in a centred box, 1424 px by default, shown here in a 1920 × 1080 window: the run's line, the jobs and the summary sit inside it, the toolbar above stays full width. The box's side edges are dragged symmetrically from 920 px to the width there is; it is one setting with the item page's box, so dragging either sets both, kept on this device. Its edges are drawn only while hovered, dragged or focused; in a window narrower than the box it takes the whole width. The edge between the jobs and the summary is a splitter, drawn here hovered: the column's line lights up in accent while hovered, dragged or focused, as the sidebar's and the item panel's do. Dragging it, or ←/→ on the focused edge, sets the jobs column from 200 to 480 px, 268 by default, kept on this device. The key bar along the bottom shows only at this overview: ⌥J/⌥K step through the jobs, ↵ opens the log, Esc goes back to Deploy, O opens GitHub. Once a job's log is open, the log's own toolbar takes over.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "J8Gad",
                  "name": "W34 · A passing run, opened at its summary",
                  "clip": true,
                  "width": 1920,
                  "height": 1080,
                  "fill": "$bg",
                  "cornerRadius": 10,
                  "stroke": "$border",
                  "strokeWidth": 1,
