                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The map of ten at the top of the summary, always whole, read as the stack's contents. It pushes where the pull request stands, its reviews and checks down; the summary scrolls on its own once it runs past the window (here Checks is cut by the bottom). The timeline keeps its place and width. Without a stack the map isn't there. The old page gave the map a 300 px column of its own on the left, taken from the main column; that column is gone.",
