            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ShEcf",
              "name": "Group note",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Drawn in the tabs layout. One repository with a few branches (fitloop/webapp) and one with many (nuxt/nuxt, 67 branches, 339 tags). A row reads in two lines beside its place in the graph: on line 1 the headline, then right after it the pull request and its CI; on line 2 the branches and tags at it, the author (avatar and name), the age and the short sha (CH64), which a list narrower than 640 px leaves out (CH65). Rows alternate with a very faint stripe, so a dot far to the left is easy to follow to its row. Each branch's lane has its own colour, eight of them in turn (CH61), and its commits' dots take it; the default branch runs on the left in a neutral light grey; a merge is a hollow dot with a dimmed headline. A divider between the graph and the rows can be dragged; lanes that don't fit fold.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
