                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "rlDzy",
                  "name": "Why",
                  "fill": "$fg-2",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 940,
                  "content": "Eight hues, no red or amber (they mean failing and running) and no indigo (the accent is the selection ring, so a lane in it would swallow the ring). Ordered so neighbouring lanes differ most; the ninth open lane takes colour 1 again. All between 5.7:1 and 8.1:1, mid saturation, so they sit under the red and amber marks. The default branch keeps the light grey it has today (graph-line-main): the trunk reads as the neutral line the coloured branches leave and join, and it can't be mistaken for one of them. A folded lane (CH44, CH45) is not a branch, so the fold and the dots on it stay neutral: the fold in graph-line, the dimmer grey, the dots on it in graph-line-main.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 12.5,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "T5VTAK",
          "name": "Group header",
          "width": 1400,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": [
            40,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "EMNd5",
              "name": "Group title",
              "fill": "$fg",
              "content": "3 · The branch and tag list",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 22,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "k9veH",
              "name": "Group note",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "On the left of the graph, under the header: always there on a wide window, and below about 1200 px it folds away and B opens it over the graph from the left. Its edge resizes it from 200 to 480 px, 280 by default, kept on this device; on a small window it gives way down to 200 px so the graph keeps 400 px. Every branch and tag on GitHub, the default branch first, then branches and tags, nested by / into folders (CH53), each group newest first or by name (CH60), each branch with its pull request and CI where it has them; each level draws its first twenty and a Show N more row for the rest. B puts the cursor in its filter; typing narrows both groups; ↵ or a click scrolls the graph to the commit, selects it there and goes back to the graph. The graph is never narrowed to one branch.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
