              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "i8xib",
                  "name": "Caption",
                  "width": 640,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 4,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "EY2NA",
                      "name": "Caption title",
                      "fill": "$fg",
                      "content": "CH53 · Folders in the branch and tag list",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "E9iRW",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Names nest by / into folders, like a file tree, as deep as the names go (release/2026/q4 is release › 2026 › q4). A prefix shared by two refs or more at a level makes a folder; one only a single ref has makes none, and that ref stays a loose row under its full name (fix/booking-tz, not a fix folder of one). A folder row: chevron, folder, name, the count of refs inside, folded or unfolded with a click or ↵. Inside a group, folders come first, then loose refs, each newest first; a folder sorts by its newest ref. A ref in a folder is indented and shows its name past the folder's path, its full name on hover (feature/login). Each level draws its first 20 entries and a Show N more row of its own for the next 20, so a hundred testing/v… tags never flood the list. While filtering, folders holding a match unfold on their own, matched rows show their full names, and the rest hide (CH17, CH25); clearing the filter brings back what the user had folded.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
