                      "content": "? lists them. Nothing new for J and K; [ ] for files and N ⇧N for threads; x { } select as in the brief; V ticks; ↓ ↑ move the line cursor stop by stop, a whole row in split, PageDown PageUp a screen at a time (CR120–CR126); E shows 20 more hidden lines of the gap nearest the cursor each time it's pressed, the whole gap from the command menu (D42; ⇧E stays Re-run failed checks); C comments on the cursor's line (CR120), and R replies to the focused thread. The two columns take VS Code's ⌘B and ⌥⌘B. Find in the diff takes VS Code's keys (CR137–CR143): ⌘F opens the bar, ⌘G ⇧⌘G and F3 ⇧F3 walk the matches from anywhere in the review, ↵ ⇧↵ do the same while the field has focus, Esc in the field closes it. Inside a comment box ⌘G stays Suggest a change.",
