                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The pointer over the right half of an added line, line 51, puts the cursor on the row: both halves take the cursor's tint over their own fill, and each half shows a comment button between its number and the code, as on github.com: the right one after 51, the left one on the empty half at the same place, both commenting on line 51. The gutter is there on every row, so the code never shifts. Hovering anywhere in a file makes it current (D44), so V, Space and C act on what is under the pointer. A click on a button comments on its line (CR90); a drag along the numbers or ⇧click still makes a range (CR73). The code stays selectable as text.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
