                      "id": "Um0CK",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Aa, ab and .* sit in the field as toggles, the file filter's .* (CR28) three times over: off by default, each flipped by a click, remembered across sessions. Flipping one searches again at once from the cursor's row, so a match that still matches stays current. All three on here, hunting placeholders left in the code: fo+\\b is a JavaScript regular expression, one line at a time, matched case-sensitively and as a whole word, so foo is marked and Foo (the case), food and for (whole words) aren't. 1 of 12: the first match at or after the cursor, on line 42.",
