                      "content": "The same bar in unified, at the top right of the narrower diff beside the conversation. A row is one line, so every match is marked once: deleted lines take their marks over the red, added over the green. Each line counts once in either layout, so the total is the same as in split; only the order inside a changed block follows the rows — all its deleted lines, then its added ones. Here the current match is the fifth, on the added line 46, where the cursor lands. Switching layout keeps the query and the current match.",
